A||||7||FieroBUZZ||Saturn manifold studs...BOOHOO!||||8||
Z||000000||FieroBUZZ||07-17-2001||05:44 PM||||I went merrily off to the Saturn dealer to buy studs for my new 2.8.  The studs could be ordered (CDN 65Cents), but that sounds too cheap for stainless.  The part number for the nuts had changed and the new nuts are....ta..da...8 Dollars each.<P>I don't suppose anyone knows the corrct size (thread, pitch, strength, etc) so I can go to the nuts and bolts R us place?<BR>TIA<BR>Gary<BR>86 SE<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||07-17-2001||06:07 PM||||You think thats bad?  My Pressure plate bolts (tiny little 8mm bolts) were 7.50$ a PIECE!!  Cause they were hardened 10.9 hardness!!!  $hit man the dealer sucks!  I had to buy 6 of the little buggers AND they didnt come with washers!!!<P>------------------<BR>      <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">        <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||07-17-2001||06:09 PM||||The diameter of the Fiero exhaust manifold bolts + studs is 8mm, I believe.  Don't recall what the pitch is, but they are a  pretty common thread.<P>1.0 pitch or 1.5 pitch or something like that?  I'm not very good with metric threads and grades (yet).<BR>   <BR>Somebody on this Forum will probably know.<P>I'm thinking that the nuts can be pretty much any decent nut (of the same thread).  Take one of the old bolts or stud with you to the hardware, and find nuts to match.  The strength of the stud / bolt is much more critical than the nut. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||07-17-2001||09:59 PM||||Don't go to the nuts and bolts section, you may get the correct size but you don't know what kind of steel they are. Go to the Fiero store and buy them there. Thats where I got mine and when you get them you will see that they are not like you get at nuts and bolts section. I think they were $1.46 each.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||07-17-2001||10:06 PM||||I'm pretty sure the exhaust manifold bolts and studs are M8 x 1.25 pitch.  The bolts are about 26 mm long, the studs are a little longer. <P>I bought mine at Pep-Boys.  I'm pretty sure they were 10.9 grade too.  I do remember wearing out several hacksaw blades cutting the heads off of three of the bolts (to make studs for the front manifold.  I think the bolts were about 79 cents each, less for the nuts. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||07-17-2001||10:29 PM||||i just bought saturn manifold studs and flange nuts, last month.  i got 12 studs and 18 flange nuts for less than $15!<P>i don't have the part numbers handy, but they are on a thread that i posted back in february or march (which was the last time i did this).  i've done Ed's fix on both my cars now, and am extreemly happy with the price and durability.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000006||StuGood||07-18-2001||10:58 AM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>...i don't have the part numbers handy, but they are on a thread that i posted back in february or march (which was the last time i did this)...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here it is, I believe: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008648.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008648.html</A> <P>BTW, I just called the 2 Saturn dealers in Wichita, and asked about exhaust manifold studs and nuts for Saturn.  They indicated the following.<P>Studs:<BR> PN 21 006 951  M8x1.25x50mm  $0.66 each<P>The three nut PN's in the above link showed up as "bad" part numbers (obsolete?), according to the dealer's parts man; but said that the following showed up as the mating part:  <P>Nuts:<BR> PN 21 006 315 (M8x1.25)      $0.51 each<P>Incidentally, both Saturn dealerships gave identical prices for the parts.  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||07-18-2001||08:19 PM||||If you want stainless hardware for stuff try a marine supply shop. check diferant shops. prices vary greatly.||||reg||1
